    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Class that reduces an F4 matrix represented as a <ref refid="class_quad_matrix" kindref="compound">QuadMatrix</ref>. The answer that you get is the submatrix that contains new pivots.</para>
<para>All <ref refid="class_quad_matrix" kindref="compound">QuadMatrix</ref> parameters passed into methods on this class are assumed to have a permutation of the top rows and left columns so that the top left matrix is upper unitriangular. In this way the lower left part of the matrix becomes all-zero after row reduction. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
